    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:2e780f63f4172747",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "63b68563bc4959bb0efef6a9511638df2ffffc1c0ce25188a0d05d89850b890c",
      "text": "Day 7 · In the morning, an excursion by private boat to the famous Marble Caves (Catedrales de Mármol): extraordinary formations sculpted over thousands of years by the waters of Lago General Carrera, their swirling blue and white chambers among the most photographed sights in Patagonia.\n\nThe journey then continues along the Carretera Austral back to Balmaceda Airport for a regional flight to Punta Arenas with DAP Airlines (Aerovías DAP). On arrival in Punta Arenas, a ground transfer takes you to Puerto Natales, gateway to Torres del Paine.\n\nHotel Altiplánico Puerto Natales\n\nHotels as listed or similar, standard rooms, breakfast basis.",
      "provenance": {
